WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<b></b>

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:18.450
<i>Even when the drought of the Kan'ei Era paid us a visit, this well had remained unfazed, but now...{</i>

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.620
Ah, hello, good sir from Aoiya.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.870
Mrs. Oshige, how is your condition?

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:35.340
The rainy season has yet to come, and the heat is quite strong.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.540
It would be dreadful if it fails to rain soon.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.780
<i>People are praying for rain...</i>

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.980
<i>What has happened to the Eastern rain?</i>

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>The Chief of Internal Affairs was assassinated in Tokyo...</i>

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.020
<i>Soujiro Seta of Shishio's Faction was the one who struck him down.</i>

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.230
<i>What of Makoto Shishio?</i>

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.060
<i>Sir, he and several subordinates have come to Kyoto.</i>

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.200
Sorry to trouble you with this upon your arrival in Kyoto, Mr. Fujita.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.200
It's fine.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.040
Makoto Shishio. Born in Shingetsu Village...

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.280
He was allied with the Choshu Faction.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.870
This man inherited his predecessor's job as a manslayer from the shadows.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.010
But I thought that he was killed in the Boshin War.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:27.130
Makoto Shishio is a treacherous individual whose lust for ambition and conquest is beyond comprehension for normal men.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.750
Some of his assassinations were of such great importance...

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.190
...that if they were brought to light, they could uproot the very foundation of the Meiji government.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.610
Had Shishio survived to greet the new era...

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.780
...there would have been a possibility that he would take advantage of such weaknesses...

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.950
...allowing him to hold Japan in the palm of his hand.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:52.180
As such, the government took advantage of the chaos in the Boshin War to dispose of him.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.060
They claim to have doused his dead body in oil and set it on fire...

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.350
B-But he still managed to live?!

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.390
He may indeed be... a ghost.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.700
Absorbed in his hatred and desire for vengeance, he has forgotten that he is still human.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.300
At any rate,<i> he</i> will most likely be the key to defeating Shishio.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.570
<i>He</i> meaning?

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:20.070
When <i>he</i> moves, so moves the era.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.450
<i>And Aoshi has been missing since?</i>

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.970
<i>The person Aoshi encountered while in Tokyo...</i>

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.750
<i>That man is also making his way to Kyoto.</i>

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.930
<i>I see. He must be chasing after Shishio as well.</i>

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.480
<i>Do you know of him?</i>

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:38.220
<i>Yes, his name is...</i>

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.760
Misao!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:49.980
As a spy of the Oniwaban group, could you try to eavesdrop on a conversation or two more appropriately?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:53.900
Tell me!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.780
Tell me about the guy who was with Lord Aoshi!

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.080
If I find him, I'll find Lord Aoshi!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.420
His name is...

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.960
...Himura.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.590
<i>Kenshin...</i>

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.370
<i>I can't let you handle defeating Shishio all on your own!</i>

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.920
<i>Battousai the Manslayer...</i>

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.400
<i>If it is still within you to speak of the restorations...</i>

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.240
<i>Then I dare you to sing of this nation's future.</i>

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:50.870
New Kyoto Arc

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.320
<i>Himura... the Battousai!</i>

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.820
I-I'm just fine, Lu No. 1!

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.660
Well, I get that you're afraid.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.500
After all, we're going up against Himura the Battousai.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.370
Formerly an imperialist for the Choshu Faction...

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.170
...he was feared as the <i>Battousai the Manslayer</i> during the end of the revolution.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.790
Supposedly the land of death spreads to wherever he goes.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.270
<i>A cross-shaped scar?</i>

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.110
He's short and skinny.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.380
Is that wimpy-looking guy really Himura?

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.200
You're right!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.290
As a member of the Oniwaban group, I have to verify that he is the enemy.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.310
Go, Lu No. 1!

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.120
Lu No. 1?!

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.970
Hey, you are tickling me, you are!

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:35.630
<i>I can't believe Lu No. 1 warmed up to him just like that!</i>

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.410
Now then, what is it that you wanted of me?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.770
Himura the Battousai, tell me!

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.400
Where is Lord Aoshi?!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.450
You know him, don't you?

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.150
I know, right?

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:57.760
He is a spy in the Oniwaban group that defended the lmperial Castle in Edo.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.190
Hey! Wait for me!

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.650
How the heck... did you get across this?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.650
<i>I won't let him go!</i>

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.540
I do not know what your relationship to Aoshi is.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:41.530
But going down a path of chaos will only lead to danger for you.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.500
Who are you to tell me that?!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.540
You should sever your feelings for that man and forget about him.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.740
It is for your own good.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.990
Don't you dare give me that crap!

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:04.690
I can't forget him!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.070
That's why I'm searching for him!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.370
Don't be crazy! Stop!

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.390
How the heck could forgetting about the person I care for the most make me happy?!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.800
Until you tell me...

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.370
I won't leave your side.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.640
I swear it!

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.610
Ahead, there is a residence...

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.370
Is that where Lord Aoshi is?

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.980
...where Makoto Shishio is.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:01.480
The man we sent on reconnaissance claims to have seen Himura the Battousai at Hakone Pass.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.920
Unfortunately, that is where he lost sight of him.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.590
What became of that man?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.820
I wound up killing him.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:10.760
Mr. Seta!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.390
You look troubled. What is it?

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:14.930
About that...

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.610
Please, this way.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.740
You brought a woman?

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.650
The hot springs located here in Shingetsu Village soothes my burns.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.080
It also helps to <i>tighten</i> the ladies up.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:35.440
Wh-Where exactly are you referring?

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:40.990
This village I believe it was your birthplace, was it not, Makoto Shishio?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.900
It's no surprise that my predecessor knows me well.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:48.700
Shingetsu Village was exploited by the
government, turning it into a ghost town.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.870
Even this therapeutic hot springs resort was an unfortunate legacy that financially destroyed the village.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.830
This village reflects the reality of the Meiji government.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.940
Just as my body reflects Meiji's true character.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.350
However, my motives are hardly driven by something as trivial as vengeance.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.150
What I seek is power.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.050
I want to create a powerful country.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.710
This world we live in now is nothing but a facade.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.350
Even though the Shogunate was replaced by a bureaucracy, nothing has actually changed.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:23.190
They use false pretenses of peace as bait, grow fat on their profits, and secretly dispose of those whom they find to be a nuisance.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.500
These are only though temporary measures.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.060
The government is rotten to the core.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.340
In order to create a new world that
is not a facade, strong power is-

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.970
So you're planning to destroy this country yet again so that you may pull the government from its roots and plant a new seed?

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.430
That is correct.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.560
This body of mine has made me accept the truth.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.460
The ruling law of this world is that <i>the strong eat the flesh of the weak.</i>

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:51.720
In that case, I will use my power to destroy all those sloths and burn away all falsehood!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:58.500
This false world may be the one to suffer as you engulf it in those flames...

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:05.450
But I cannot allow you to fill this era with the screams of the innocent who are now living in peace!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:12.510
Your sword... Didn't Shakku Arai forge it in his final days?

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:13.920
This one here is the same.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.880
Which makes them brother swords.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:22.420
However, Shakku created my sword purely to kill when he forged this blade.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:28.260
In comparison, your sword that cannot kill is no different than our current era.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.430
It was merely a created out of confusion.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.200
It can't kill?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.800
Our swords match their owners.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:40.280
In which case, the relationship you and I share
is that of brothers who are complete opposites.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.610
It's okay, then?

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:46.310
Yeah, play with him for me.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.250
It is too soon for a showdown between <i>brothers.</i>

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:51.610
Then, I won't hesitate to....

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.250
Will Sou be all right on his own?

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.550
Don't worry.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:06.060
His strength comes directly from his lack of emotions.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.600
Does that mean you can't read his mind?

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.900
Going up against the Hiten Mitsurugi style, he could prove to be the ultimate foe.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.780
The Battoujutsu, which would give him the lead, may prove effective.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:20.950
Because he lacks sorrow, he feels nothing in his heart about killing men...

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:26.990
How will the Battousai and his halfhearted oath to not kill perform against Soujiro's blade?

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.990
Actually, he is no longer the Battousai.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.490
It is clear how this battle will end.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.990
Victory goes to me, doesn't it?

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:55.540
No, it's a draw!

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.680
Wow, this is amazing!

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:02.180
Oh well. It was Mr. Shishio's anyway.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.460
This match doesn't have a winner or a loser.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.910
I'll excuse myself for today now...

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.750
...but I hope you'll fight me again.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.800
And have a new sword ready by the time I see you again.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:18.040
Just so you know, Shakku isn't alive anymore.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.830
Himura...

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.880
What are you going to do?

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.520
I'm fine here, I am.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:34.690
If you didn't have the money to cover two rooms, we didn't have to stay here.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:38.530
In your search for <i>this one</i>, you never stopped running, not even to sleep.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.220
Your feet cannot take much more...

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:44.970
Don't make fun of me!

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.200
I am not making fun of you...

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.410
You know that you are!

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:53.180
If everything was right in the world, I would be a female ninja, working by Lord Aoshi's side.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:56.250
And I could tell going by your stances.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:13:00.440
There is no way you could possibly lose to that Soujiro guy!

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.380
He said that you can't kill.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.880
And then there's your reverse-blade sword...

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.560
Are you seriously trying not to kill anyone?

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.560
He called you his predecessor...

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.150
Who exactly is this Makoto Shishio?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:21.570
It was because of <i>this one</i>, that his fate was thrown off course, it was.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:28.580
Even if one darkness were to vanish, there would be another to take its place.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.570
I thought I understood that, and yet...

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.650
The night birds... are crying out.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:40.820
Indeed, they are.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:42.420
For me...

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.090
Ever since I was little, for some reason, I've been afraid of the night.

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:53.100
But when I was next to Lord Aoshi, I was fine.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:59.810
Lord Aoshi always goes on ahead, telling me what lies ahead in the darkness.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.140
Your name?

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:05.440
I never told you?

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:06.530
Misao!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.160
I'm Misao Makimachi.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:15.850
If you continue to be involved with <i>this one's </i>affairs, 
Miss Misao, it will only feed the darkness that frightens you so.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.090
If it's for Lord Aoshi, I don't care!

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.810
It's not like I'm doing him any favors or anything.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.840
But I have to find out about this Shishio guy anyway.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.880
Lu No. 1.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.480
What gives?!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.860
Why isn't there a single teahouse around here?

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.520
Yahiko, that sounds pathetic.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:54.460
I can't believe we got off at Owari Port!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.560
You should find out what the destination is when you choose a ship.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.770
This is part of our training.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:03.510
As we are right now, wouldn't we just be getting in Kenshin's way?

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.870
Then maybe we shouldn't have come to begin with!

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.410
That's...

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.970
Geez!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.810
C'mon! C'mon! You look pathetic, Kaoru!

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.250
Your feet aren't moving!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.660
Yahiko!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.090
Good evening!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.830
Good evening!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.170
No one's home?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.040
Wow, he's got a bunch of stuff!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.830
This is all pottery.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.650
But, this thing is covered in cracks!

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.210
These aren't good. The person sucks at doing this.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.290
It broke...

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.510
Forgive us.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.350
We came inside uninvited.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:16:00.100
The veins of pottery teach us the laws of the human world.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.670
I dropped it 'cause you startled me.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:05.400
Sorry about that, old-!

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:07.670
Yahiko!

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.700
You shall pay with your body.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.580
Hot!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:18.280
So hot! You're burning me!

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.780
I'm dying!

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:20.920
You want to die?

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:23.220
That's okay! I don't care if I die!

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.220
You can't! I will force you to live.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.790
This heat is the warmth of life.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.260
I shall use it to burn away the rotten government!

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:38.930
With the heat of life, I will bring Kyoto and our lethargic era to a boil.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.610
To think you planned your strike for when I was enjoying myself, Usui.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:51.360
Hardly!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.280
My Mind's Eye cannot perceive actions of this nature.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.620
It merely worked out that way.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:56.620
Really!

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.490
I have a job for you since you have interrupted our fun.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:03.950
Hajime Saito, a former member of the Shinsengumi, is sniffing around our trail.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.730
Keep an eye on him.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.570
And what of Himura the Battousai?

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.500
I am not interested in one soon to die.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:10.630
Understood.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:16.200
That man still hopes to take your life, Lord Shishio.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.000
It's best that way.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:21.680
This is where those with power gather.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.750
There are those who I have saved, those who serve me...

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.850
...those who rely on me, those who use me...

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.310
...and those who are burning with the desire to kill me after suffering defeat by my hands.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:36.320
But only true power, even if it be evil, could keep this group together.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.400
Lord Shishio...

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.990
If you are strong you live, and if you are weak you die.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:45.200
As such, I simply need to be the strongest.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:51.300
Nothing may strike fear into the man who will
burn down the era with the flame called <i>power.</i>

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:57.410
Shakku's last sword, ya say?

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:01.150
Yes, although I am certain he will catch wind of it as well.

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.420
What say you, Mr. Chou?

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.980
Does it get your excited as a sword collector?

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:11.130
You bet it does, but there ain't no way Shishio's gonna let me face Himura the Battousai.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:13.430
It's fine. Do whatever you want.

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.470
Shishio!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.440
It was not Himura's reverse-blade sword that broke...

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.270
...but his beliefs.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:27.110
Miss Misao, <i>this one</i>...

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.510
It's fine, it's fine! Just you leave this to me.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.750
Lu No. 1!

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.620
It's from Okina!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:46.390
<i>Shakku had a son with whom he entrusted all of his arts.</i>

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.900
<i>His name is Seiku Arai.</i>

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.200
Hello.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:59.910
I am sorry, but may I humbly turn down that commission?

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.780
What?! Why?!

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:08.880
My father used to say, <i>I will create a new world with my swords.</i>

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:17.120
But the swords my father created under that philosophy stole the lives of many who carried the weight of the new era.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:19.720
It's the Meiji Era now.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.390
The age of peace has finally come.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.830
Samurai have abandoned their swords.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:30.160
Therefore, I wish to abandon my work as a swordsmith.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:33.570
This is an age of peace?

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.570
Yes.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.620
What were you making, may I ask?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:46.080
Oh, it is a pellet drum for Iori, my son.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.850
Really, I'm embarrassed by how poorly it turned out.

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:52.450
I don't seem to have a knack for it like I do with forging blades.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:56.120
Oh, it's a little bent.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.140
I apologize for having asked the impossible.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:03.370
Mr. Himura?

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.270
<i>We ones</i> shall excuse ourselves.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.850
B-But, hey you!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.810
What are you going to do without a reverse-blade sword?!

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:12.180
Hey, Himura!

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.400
Step into it quicker.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.030
Don't rely upon your arm strength!

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.600
You won't finish before lunch at this rate.

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.500
Damn it!

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:32.360
Really, why must we do this?

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:36.170
We don't have time for this crap!

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.910
<i>That man...</i>

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.740
We need to hurry and find Kenshin.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:48.910
Are you learning the sword from Kenshin Himura?

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:50.810
Don't be stupid!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.640
My sword is that of the Kamiya Kasshin style!

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:56.160
Its sword is meant to protect.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.660
Don't lump it together with Battoujutsu!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.850
Then why are you chasing after him?

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:03.500
Well, it's obvious!

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:07.570
I can't leave that goofball to his own devices.

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:13.240
Kenshin... Do you know Kenshin?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.100
That's right! How do you know him?

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.580
My goodness...

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:39.570
Tonight, we party!

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.270
But weren't you just drinking?

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:46.210
While away from his master, my pupil has been growing and maturing.

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:49.210
It is a rather pleasing thought.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:56.050
He has finally obtained what he once lacked in his swordsmanship.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.040
Wait up!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:01.170
You can't fight without a sword, can you?

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:06.730
Sir Seiku lives in an age of peace.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:09.760
It is not my right to destroy that peace, it is not.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:10.990
Yeah, but...

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:13.090
A-Are you all right?

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:17.330
What's the matter?

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:27.720
I-Io... Iori was taken from me!

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:28.980
What?!

00:22:29.190 --> 00:22:29.950
Why?!

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:31.530
Why would someone do that?!

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:37.860
He wanted your father's last sword... and then he-!

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:44.070
This happened... because <i>this one</i> wanted a reverse-blade sword.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:46.370
What are you talking about?

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.470
This and that are two different-

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:54.210
Himura?

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:56.980
The poor thing!

00:22:57.350 --> 00:23:02.020
To think they dumped Shakku's last work out in such a remote place.

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.490
Watch it! Don't pull my hair.

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:08.390
Dang, I don't much care for babies.

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:12.500
If you keep hurtin' me like that, then I'll cut you down in one strike!

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:14.430
Broom! Broom!

00:23:14.430 --> 00:23:15.770
I seriously don't like ya.

00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:17.230
Iori!

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:18.870
Iori!

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:20.370
Let the child go.

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:21.870
Mr. Himura...

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:26.330
I see. So I take it yer the infamous Battousai the Manslayer?

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:29.800
You want Shakku's last piece, right?

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:31.750
Well I'm just shakin' in my boots.

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:42.820
I'm gonna kill ya right quick and then try out Shakku's famous blade on that baby!

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:45.990
Himura, you don't have a sword!

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:54.370
He's using his sheath against someone with a sword?

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:57.500
I must never offer the sword to that man...

00:23:58.480 --> 00:23:59.620
Mr. Himura's eyes...

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.580
The light shining from them has vanished!

00:24:03.610 --> 00:24:08.610
Mr. Himura's eyes had seemed so gentle, yet this battle has turned him into a demon!

00:24:13.160 --> 00:24:15.920
Battousai the Manslayer...

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:19.220
Hey, weren't ya against killin' people?

00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:21.230
I will not kill you.

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:24.630
So ya can do anything ya want so long as it don't kill me?

00:24:24.640 --> 00:24:26.310
Ain't you nice!

00:24:27.240 --> 00:24:29.440
It was <i>this one's</i> job to fight...

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:33.430
...but somewhere along the line, I forced the tainted name of a manslayer on Shishio.

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:35.610
Himura!

00:24:35.610 --> 00:24:39.880
But now... <i>this one</i> shall accept the taint unto <i>this one's</i> self...

00:24:40.420 --> 00:24:43.050
A taint needed to protect a world of peace.

00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:46.260
N-No! That is just-

00:24:46.260 --> 00:24:47.880
A contradiction.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:56.430
Iori!

00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:57.800
Thank goodness!

00:24:57.800 --> 00:24:59.000
Iori...

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:01.160
That was really awesome.

00:25:03.040 --> 00:25:07.480
If yer totally empty-handed, I can actually stand a chance!

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:20.150
<i>The taint... needed to defend the</i>
<i>peace and protect our loved ones...</i>

00:25:27.230 --> 00:25:31.330
<i>Father, I... I want to defend our peace!</i>

00:25:32.470 --> 00:25:34.770
<i>But... But...</i>

00:25:42.080 --> 00:25:45.080
Now ya can't run around and dodge my blows, can ya?

00:25:45.080 --> 00:25:46.450
Mr. Himura!

00:25:51.820 --> 00:25:52.480
For you...!

00:25:52.820 --> 00:25:54.570
This blade was meant<i> for you!</i>

00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:57.860
That is Shakku's final masterpiece.

00:25:58.730 --> 00:26:00.700
B-But...

00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:03.600
Isn't this...

00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:05.040
...a reverse-blade sword?!

00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:06.570
River-blade sword!

00:26:06.570 --> 00:26:10.340
Sir Shakku, I shall live by your ideals, I shall!

00:26:11.110 --> 00:26:12.410
What?!

00:26:23.390 --> 00:26:25.150
Himura, you did it!

00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:29.430
Yeah, it's okay. Broom Head didn't die.

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:31.300
Broom! Broom!

00:26:31.300 --> 00:26:34.530
I'm definitely going to make sure that you get turned over to the police.

00:26:41.100 --> 00:26:42.270
It will be okay.

00:26:42.270 --> 00:26:45.540
The unvarnished wood simply couldn't withstand the power of your attack.

00:26:50.810 --> 00:26:55.340
<i>Slaying myself, my forged blades amass...</i>

00:26:55.990 --> 00:26:59.720
<i>Hated by my child, I do this for my grandchild's future.</i>

00:27:00.420 --> 00:27:05.890
After seeing you in battle, Mr. Himura, I believe I understand my father a little better.

00:27:06.630 --> 00:27:12.020
This reverse-blade sword represents the way you, Mr. Himura, and my father lived.

00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:25.570
Mr. Himura, my father longed for the coming of
a peaceful world more than anyone, didn't he?

00:27:26.520 --> 00:27:29.920
Yet even so, he lived amidst the turmoil during the revolution.

00:27:30.350 --> 00:27:33.690
He could neither pull back nor stop to consider his actions.

00:27:33.690 --> 00:27:36.220
He had no choice but to continue making swords to kill.

00:27:36.660 --> 00:27:41.500
He had no choice but to go directly against his wishes... to live a contradicting life.

00:27:42.100 --> 00:27:48.230
Yet even so, he accepted that contradicting
lifestyle because he wished to protect someone.

00:27:48.710 --> 00:27:50.830
Isn't that right, Mr. Himura?

00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:53.300
Sir Seiku...

00:27:56.350 --> 00:27:58.030
The reverse-blade sword, Keishin.

00:27:58.690 --> 00:27:59.740
Please take it with you!

00:28:00.120 --> 00:28:02.420
I believe that is what my father would have wanted.

00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:09.320
At this time, it is what <i>this one</i> needs most of all.

00:28:09.630 --> 00:28:11.290
I humbly accept your kind offer, that I do.

00:28:11.830 --> 00:28:12.710
Himura!

00:28:12.710 --> 00:28:14.080
I doo! I doo!

00:28:14.080 --> 00:28:16.170
Himura I doo!

00:28:17.130 --> 00:28:18.460
He's saying, "I do"!

00:28:53.330 --> 00:28:55.520
For now, let's go to Aoiya!

00:28:56.030 --> 00:28:58.120
I'll introduce you to Gramps and the others.

00:28:58.670 --> 00:29:01.000
I am confident they will help...

00:29:02.300 --> 00:29:03.410
Himura?

00:29:03.410 --> 00:29:06.000
It is time we parted ways, it is, Miss Misao.

00:29:08.340 --> 00:29:11.970
From this point on, <i>this one</i> must fight this battle on his own.

00:29:13.750 --> 00:29:18.150
Miss Misao, I must not draw you further into my affairs.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:19.940
What are you talking about?

00:29:19.940 --> 00:29:23.190
This is nothing and I don't care if I get caught up in this.

00:29:24.560 --> 00:29:25.740
Th-That's right!

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:28.530
You still haven't told me anything about Lord Aoshi!

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:33.460
Han'nya...

00:29:35.370 --> 00:29:37.970
Shikijo, Beshimi and Hyottoko...

00:29:38.570 --> 00:29:40.180
Those are the guys from the Oniwaban!

00:29:40.180 --> 00:29:42.640
All of them are dead.

00:29:47.380 --> 00:29:48.580
No way!

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:52.790
All of them? Because they got tangled up with you?

00:29:52.790 --> 00:29:54.290
But you don't kill people, right?

00:29:54.290 --> 00:29:57.230
I did not directly bring an end their lives...

00:29:58.290 --> 00:30:05.360
But even so, if they had not chosen to fight me,
their lives would not have been lost.

00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:11.570
Himura the Battousai!

00:31:07.990 --> 00:31:09.930
I'm home!

00:31:11.700 --> 00:31:13.290
Misao!

00:31:16.140 --> 00:31:17.370
What's going on?

00:31:17.370 --> 00:31:19.910
Oh, well, uh, you see...

00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:20.730
Where's Gramps?

00:31:20.730 --> 00:31:22.630
If-If you mean Okina...

00:31:32.920 --> 00:31:34.550
Misao...

00:31:34.720 --> 00:31:37.260
Answer me. Come on, Omasu!

00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:38.990
Where did Gramps go?

00:31:40.490 --> 00:31:44.600
If Gramps pulled out his old shinobi uniform and weapons...

00:31:44.600 --> 00:31:46.330
...then this has to be something serious!

00:31:48.700 --> 00:31:50.790
The preparations are complete.

00:31:51.170 --> 00:31:52.940
I've burdened you.

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:56.380
If it is within the capacity of a woman such as I, who cannot fight...

00:31:56.380 --> 00:31:57.410
I will do anything.

00:31:57.410 --> 00:31:59.610
I have faith in my subordinates.

00:31:59.610 --> 00:32:03.340
But I could not entrust this to anyone but you.

00:32:03.720 --> 00:32:05.250
I can leave everything in your able hands.

00:32:05.250 --> 00:32:09.380
You chose me not for my appearance, but for who I am.

00:32:10.220 --> 00:32:11.710
Lord Shishio...

00:32:16.630 --> 00:32:18.760
That certainly took you a while.

00:32:18.760 --> 00:32:21.160
Slaying fifty men took some time.

00:32:21.700 --> 00:32:24.600
I merely said to keep an eye on Saito.

00:32:24.770 --> 00:32:26.540
I was not on a child's errand.

00:32:26.540 --> 00:32:28.550
I merely did this on the side.

00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:34.540
Fifty men... As you can imagine, I am still throbbing with excitement!

00:32:35.410 --> 00:32:38.050
May I request a reward for completing my errand?

00:32:38.050 --> 00:32:39.950
Yeah, but of course.

00:32:40.490 --> 00:32:42.780
I have no interest in taking this country!

00:32:43.260 --> 00:32:45.760
All I want is to take your life!

00:32:45.760 --> 00:32:46.590
Usui!

00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:47.790
Very well.

00:32:48.090 --> 00:32:53.290
It is a man's privilege to take that
which he desires with his own might.

00:32:53.470 --> 00:32:55.130
I shall face you.

00:32:56.130 --> 00:32:59.000
I just so happened to be itching for a fight myself.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.030
Let us fight until we are fully satisfied.

00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:02.800
Lord Shishio!

00:33:10.120 --> 00:33:12.410
How are things with you, Himura?

00:33:13.350 --> 00:33:15.320
Hajime Saito.

00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:20.590
Rumor has it that your reverse-blade sword has been broken.

00:33:20.830 --> 00:33:24.490
Even in Kyoto, do you keep your oath not to kill?

00:33:24.630 --> 00:33:29.470
Indeed, I have kept my oath. But that is all.

00:33:30.200 --> 00:33:36.740
If I could have the honor of seeing Battousai the Manslayer here in Kyoto, it would make for a most pleasant sight.

00:33:39.980 --> 00:33:45.780
Last night, the fifty police officers I enlisted
in the fight to subdue Shishio were murdered.

00:33:46.720 --> 00:33:48.950
It happened shortly after I issued their orders.

00:33:49.390 --> 00:33:51.220
Someone must have been watching me.

00:33:51.220 --> 00:33:56.430
Also, I have some information from Chou, the member of Shishio's faction that you captured this afternoon.

00:33:58.900 --> 00:34:00.630
Well then, he's all yours.

00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:07.870
I am Goro Fujita, the one placed in charge of torturing you.

00:34:07.870 --> 00:34:09.270
Hajime Saito!

00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:12.570
Didn't ya used to serve in the Shinsengumi?

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:15.180
And speakin' of Shinsengumi...

00:34:15.180 --> 00:34:22.690
Y'all are famous for putting old Mr. Furutaka under cruel torture to make him fess up before the lkeda-ya Incident.

00:34:22.690 --> 00:34:26.680
You ain't the guy who did the dirty deed, are ya?

00:34:26.930 --> 00:34:29.690
Lucky for you, you're absolutely right.

00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:34.660
This is too much! I ain't the type to tough it out.

00:34:34.770 --> 00:34:37.570
If I snitch, Lord Shishio'll kill me.

00:34:37.570 --> 00:34:41.030
So if yer willin' to protect me, I'll tell ya anything ya wanna know.

00:34:41.740 --> 00:34:44.680
Of course, I will guarantee your safety.

00:34:44.740 --> 00:34:47.180
I doubt anything could best the power of the state, right?

00:34:47.350 --> 00:34:48.270
Talk.

00:34:48.880 --> 00:34:51.020
Keep me safe!

00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:58.220
Lord Shishio's plan is based upon the scenario written by the radical loyalists from the lkeda-ya Incident.

00:34:58.860 --> 00:35:04.660
He intends to set Kyoto ablaze, assassinate the leaders of the Shogunate, and take the emperor to Choshu.

00:35:05.030 --> 00:35:10.030
It's a massive plan to set the thousand-year capital on fire since they were not able to pull it off last time.

00:35:10.770 --> 00:35:14.830
He's got five hundred subordinates who will spread fires all across Kyoto.

00:35:14.940 --> 00:35:18.710
During the confusion of the fire, they will assassinate all of the government officials in Kyoto!

00:35:18.710 --> 00:35:25.910
He has taken measures for the loyalists that burned him to get a taste of the major offense they had attempted during the end of the Shogunate.

00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:27.220
Whatcha think?

00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:30.190
Whether ya believe me or not is up to you.

00:35:30.590 --> 00:35:34.080
If it was all a load of bull, yer welcome to do whatever ya like with me!

00:35:34.730 --> 00:35:36.960
Ain't like I can run away or hide.

00:35:38.800 --> 00:35:41.100
Is that <i>all</i> you know?

00:35:41.900 --> 00:35:44.670
I have information that verifies your statement.

00:35:44.670 --> 00:35:48.900
What you said can be trusted, but I doubt that is all of it, am I right?

00:35:49.310 --> 00:35:54.970
He wants to avoid a repeat of what happened in lkeda-ya at all costs, assuming of course that Shishio is not a fool.

00:35:55.280 --> 00:35:57.610
It is only natural that you don't know more.

00:35:57.950 --> 00:36:01.890
A careless slip of the tongue, and the plan would fall to pieces.

00:36:01.990 --> 00:36:06.490
If I were in Shishio's shoes, I would <i>never</i> disclose important information like that...

00:36:06.490 --> 00:36:10.130
...especially if it could affect the success of the operation with an untrustworthy subordinate.

00:36:10.130 --> 00:36:12.530
Lord Shishio ain't like you!

00:36:12.530 --> 00:36:17.060
There's no way I woulda followed him if he was such a narrow-minded prick!

00:36:17.470 --> 00:36:20.510
Oh, so do you know what is going on behind the scenes?

00:36:20.510 --> 00:36:23.010
You bet! Everyone's in on it.

00:36:23.010 --> 00:36:25.840
But even if ya tortured me, I ain't talkin!

00:36:26.140 --> 00:36:29.270
That'd be the same as betrayin' Lord Shishio.

00:36:29.820 --> 00:36:32.480
Anyone can gloss over the truth.

00:36:33.390 --> 00:36:37.720
You cannot deny the possibility that you were fed false information.

00:36:37.720 --> 00:36:39.830
That ain't true! I saw it with my own eyes.

00:36:39.830 --> 00:36:41.420
Right in the Port of Osaka!

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:46.180
That is all I needed to know.

00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:48.510
You saved me the trouble of having to torture you.

00:36:49.070 --> 00:36:50.500
Much appreciated.

00:36:56.170 --> 00:36:57.540
The Great Kyoto Fire...

00:36:58.080 --> 00:37:05.510
He will topple the people's trust in the government by burning what has been ingrained in the hearts of the Japanese as the symbol of our capital.

00:37:06.490 --> 00:37:08.890
This is Shishio's declaration of war.

00:37:09.220 --> 00:37:12.020
As for the other scheme that he kept secret...

00:37:12.190 --> 00:37:14.080
You and I will stop him.

00:37:14.580 --> 00:37:15.500
I'm guessing you have no objections?

00:37:19.430 --> 00:37:21.960
Where is Himura the Battousai?

00:37:24.040 --> 00:37:29.010
Your desire for information on Himura has led you to attack your old hideout, Aoiya.

00:37:29.010 --> 00:37:30.980
You have grown twisted!

00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:38.050
It is too late to hammer out your distortions!

00:37:38.350 --> 00:37:39.720
I must crush you.

00:37:48.290 --> 00:37:50.860
Oh, boy. They are fighting for keeps.

00:37:50.860 --> 00:37:52.260
Sou.

00:37:53.570 --> 00:37:56.530
Do you think Shishio intends to kill him?

00:37:56.900 --> 00:37:59.770
And here Usui could prove to be a quite useful.

00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:02.200
It is fine, Sou.

00:38:02.470 --> 00:38:05.340
This is his form of justice.

00:38:09.110 --> 00:38:13.720
To stop the Great Kyoto Fire, we will need the assistance of a group that knows Kyoto well, we will.

00:38:13.990 --> 00:38:15.950
<i>This one</i> knows who to ask.

00:38:16.450 --> 00:38:19.250
<i>Fight a group with a group,</i> is what you're saying?

00:38:19.390 --> 00:38:24.260
lt'd be great if you could find replacements for the fifty men I've lost.

00:38:27.470 --> 00:38:29.430
Perhaps the outcome will prove promising...

00:38:29.430 --> 00:38:34.460
...if I further confuse a heart already in turmoil as you resist returning to your manslayer ways.

00:38:35.310 --> 00:38:37.580
Two people have followed you here from Tokyo.

00:38:37.790 --> 00:38:39.790
They have already arrived in Kyoto.

00:39:00.270 --> 00:39:01.560
I made it in...

00:39:14.310 --> 00:39:15.350
Lord Aoshi!

00:39:15.350 --> 00:39:18.250
Never show yourself to me again.

00:39:32.230 --> 00:39:33.600
How was it, Usui?

00:39:33.930 --> 00:39:35.100
Were you boiling?

00:39:35.370 --> 00:39:36.370
Yeah...

00:39:36.370 --> 00:39:37.350
We're not done yet.

00:39:37.850 --> 00:39:40.140
See how I burn before you go.

00:39:40.570 --> 00:39:44.870
I will show you directly through those festering eyes, not through your Mind's Eye.

00:39:46.040 --> 00:39:47.510
I saw it...

00:39:47.510 --> 00:39:49.010
What did you see?

00:39:49.010 --> 00:39:53.750
Your... body... as it burns in flames.

00:39:56.050 --> 00:39:58.680
That is exactly what I desire.

00:40:00.690 --> 00:40:03.230
Yahiko!

00:40:03.230 --> 00:40:06.630
Really! Where could he have gone? He ran off...

00:40:39.260 --> 00:40:42.060
Oh, Officer Fujita! What impeccable timing.

00:40:42.270 --> 00:40:45.730
I've got a man in custody who picked a massive fight in town.

00:40:45.870 --> 00:40:48.670
He's terribly insistent that I let him see you.

00:40:48.770 --> 00:40:50.930
I think he said you know each other...

00:40:56.050 --> 00:40:57.650
Just like I thought!

00:40:57.650 --> 00:41:03.080
Instead of blindly searching around, I just needed to get in trouble with the cops to catch you!

00:41:03.320 --> 00:41:06.660
Meeting up that way is a whole lot faster.

00:41:06.660 --> 00:41:09.830
So it was you after all, moron!

00:41:09.830 --> 00:41:11.760
'Course it was!

00:41:11.760 --> 00:41:15.560
This is Sanosuke Sagara's grand arrival in Kyoto!

00:41:17.670 --> 00:41:19.140
Kenshin...

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:21.970
Um, I...

00:41:21.970 --> 00:41:23.460
Why?!

00:41:23.910 --> 00:41:25.600
Why did you come?

00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:28.040
Are you... mad?

00:41:28.680 --> 00:41:29.910
Half of me is.

00:41:31.680 --> 00:41:33.580
My other half says...

00:41:35.490 --> 00:41:36.890
Thank you.

00:41:47.800 --> 00:41:49.110
You guys!

00:41:49.110 --> 00:41:51.730
Why are you enjoying some emotional reunion without me?!

00:41:51.770 --> 00:41:54.540
Because you just had to wander off somewhere!

00:41:54.540 --> 00:41:58.100
Nature called! Figure that out for yourself, Miss. Dense!

00:41:58.510 --> 00:42:01.050
Going to pee isn't all that embarrassing for a guy!

00:42:01.050 --> 00:42:03.050
Just be straightforward about it, Yahiko!

00:42:03.050 --> 00:42:04.880
I'm still going through puberty!

00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:07.820
Or so you'd like to think! You're still a little brat!

00:42:07.820 --> 00:42:10.950
You suffer embarrassment as you mature!

00:42:22.170 --> 00:42:24.660
<i>I just... don't know anymore!</i>

00:42:28.540 --> 00:42:30.440
<i>There is no stopping now!</i>

00:42:32.540 --> 00:42:35.010
<i>Neither for you, nor me...</i>

00:42:41.850 --> 00:42:45.290
<i>If you can stop me, I dare you to try!</i>

00:42:46.190 --> 00:42:48.250
<i>I can no longer turn back.</i>

00:42:49.330 --> 00:42:52.820
<i>Until I defeat him, my battle will not come to an end.</i>

00:43:06.540 --> 00:43:10.040
<i>I... will never leave your side again.</i>

00:43:14.230 --> 00:43:18.240
<i>Even if I cannot see what lays ahead, I will keep walking...</i>

00:43:18.650 --> 00:43:19.950
<i>...with this sword.</i>

00:43:42.470 --> 00:43:43.370
Hyottoko.

00:43:44.720 --> 00:43:45.450
Beshimi.

00:43:46.550 --> 00:43:47.630
Shikijo.

00:43:48.310 --> 00:43:49.260
Han'nya!

00:46:26.470 --> 00:46:30.010
How is it progressing? Are you done carving your best work yet?

00:46:30.720 --> 00:46:31.850
I'm afraid not.

00:46:33.320 --> 00:46:36.640
I haven't been inspired yet for how the Buddha's face will look to save this world.

00:46:37.760 --> 00:46:40.530
If that's the case, then it's fine to carve my face.

00:46:42.760 --> 00:46:44.640
What words would you like engraved on it?

00:46:44.840 --> 00:46:45.890
Let's see...

00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:49.650
If you are strong you live, if you are weak you die.

00:46:50.180 --> 00:46:52.060
<i>Survival of the Fittest.</i>

00:46:52.290 --> 00:46:57.410
Even though it may sound harsh, keeping it simple
is actually closer to the ultimate truth.

00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:01.500
Fuji again?

00:47:01.690 --> 00:47:07.080
It's not that simple to repress one's strength, Anji.

00:47:08.300 --> 00:47:10.930
This is Mr. Usui's grave, isn't it?

00:47:11.440 --> 00:47:14.160
Miss Yumi, you're very kind.

00:47:14.580 --> 00:47:18.870
You even mourn someone who opposed Mr. Shishio, even to the end.

00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:26.070
All of us, everyone, were originally wiped out at the beginning of the Meiji Era.

00:47:26.450 --> 00:47:31.440
Even though, each of us was persecuted by this era, and were stripped of our reasons to live...

00:47:31.540 --> 00:47:36.300
The ones who follow Mr. Shishio have been able to find that light once more.

00:47:36.590 --> 00:47:41.360
The light? Even though Mr. Shishio wiped out both of Mr. Usui's eyes?

00:47:41.770 --> 00:47:46.520
Usui's reason to live was to seek revenge against Lord Shishio.

00:47:47.250 --> 00:47:49.060
That could also be light.

00:47:49.460 --> 00:47:51.120
Not a very good one though.

00:47:51.710 --> 00:47:52.540
Lord Shishio.

00:47:53.100 --> 00:47:54.360
We're leaving.

00:47:54.600 --> 00:47:55.680
Finally, right?

00:47:56.270 --> 00:47:59.370
We're sailing off to our glory.

00:48:00.520 --> 00:48:08.190
During the Boshin war, at the Battle at Toba-Fushimi, Yoshinobu Tokugawa fled by ship from the Port of Osaka bay to Edo.

00:48:08.360 --> 00:48:11.550
Thus, this is the main reason why the Imperialists won, was because this tactic that was taken.

00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:17.410
If Shishio is trying to win with the same type of satire...

00:48:18.200 --> 00:48:21.400
...then his real target in mind must be to the east.

00:48:22.170 --> 00:48:23.500
His goal must be-

00:48:23.630 --> 00:48:24.660
Seconds!

00:48:26.770 --> 00:48:28.590
Don't say it to me! Tell that person instead.

00:48:29.260 --> 00:48:29.880
Seconds!

00:48:29.950 --> 00:48:30.630
Certainly!

00:48:30.760 --> 00:48:33.790
You came all the way to Kyoto by yourself with no food or water.

00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:35.680
I'm almost in tears.

00:48:36.070 --> 00:48:36.740
What?

00:48:36.910 --> 00:48:41.450
You and that girl must really care about him.

00:48:41.660 --> 00:48:47.400
Don't get me wrong, I didn't come to Kyoto just to help Kenshin.

00:48:48.400 --> 00:48:49.780
Here, thank you for waiting.

00:48:56.060 --> 00:48:58.790
I came here to fight in my own way...

00:48:59.290 --> 00:49:01.160
No matter who it is.

00:49:01.700 --> 00:49:05.260
I can't stand cowards who attack others from the shadows.

00:49:07.090 --> 00:49:09.560
You were a Sekihotai soldier?

00:49:09.700 --> 00:49:12.840
I can never forgive the Meiji Government either.

00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:18.220
They branded my captain traitor and then executed all of them.

00:49:23.390 --> 00:49:31.820
But if he fights the government using dirty tactics and involves innocent people who have no part in this, he's the same as them.

00:49:32.020 --> 00:49:33.440
I see.

00:49:33.770 --> 00:49:38.280
The fastest way to find this Shishio guy, is to tag along with you.

00:49:38.280 --> 00:49:41.540
Isn't it right, Shinsengumi Third Squad Leader?

00:49:45.780 --> 00:49:47.290
Well, where are we headed?

00:49:48.150 --> 00:49:52.490
Haven't those ears of your been listening to anything I said, rooster head?

00:49:52.880 --> 00:49:56.930
It's my style to only enjoy things seriously when I'm having a meal!

00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:03.130
To Osaka.

00:50:05.810 --> 00:50:06.530
Osaka?

00:50:07.070 --> 00:50:13.590
From Saito's intel, Shishio should have already left
towards there, which is his true plan.

00:50:13.920 --> 00:50:15.970
If that's so, then the Great Kyoto Fire is a deception?

00:50:16.580 --> 00:50:20.860
No. He's using most of his army here.

00:50:21.120 --> 00:50:25.240
He has something so powerful that he might possibly win with a smaller army, he has.

00:50:25.690 --> 00:50:27.200
Huh? What do you mean by that?

00:50:27.620 --> 00:50:29.520
For example a black ship.

00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:30.960
A black ship?!

00:50:31.190 --> 00:50:33.590
Well, that is just an example, it is.

00:50:33.760 --> 00:50:37.440
But, the people of Tokyo are still in fear from the arrival of the black ships.

00:50:38.080 --> 00:50:42.970
So if an ship were to appear that looked like an enemy, it's inevitable that alone would be turmoil among the people.

00:50:45.240 --> 00:50:46.090
Miss Kaoru...

00:50:46.300 --> 00:50:49.090
Why did you suddenly change your mind about telling us?

00:50:49.230 --> 00:50:55.970
I thought if I didn't tell you, I worried that you'd do something rash...

00:50:56.220 --> 00:50:57.670
What's that supposed to mean?

00:50:58.310 --> 00:51:00.020
Excuse me for being a rash woman!

00:51:00.020 --> 00:51:03.380
Oh geez. Even in Kyoto these two still argue like a couple.

00:51:04.940 --> 00:51:06.020
A messenger pigeon?

00:51:06.620 --> 00:51:07.700
It's Lu No. 1.

00:51:12.660 --> 00:51:13.690
What's wrong, Kenshin?

00:51:14.800 --> 00:51:15.540
Here you go.

00:51:16.120 --> 00:51:18.980
Sorry to impose, especially during this difficult time.

00:51:19.600 --> 00:51:24.720
It's okay. We have spare rooms. Please stay as long as you'd like.

00:51:24.980 --> 00:51:26.030
Thanks for taking care of us.

00:51:31.690 --> 00:51:33.110
So that's it, is it?

00:51:34.110 --> 00:51:35.070
It was Aoshi...

00:51:36.030 --> 00:51:42.040
The Lord Aoshi that I knew, is no longer
the same Lord Aoshi now.

00:51:43.950 --> 00:51:50.190
I don't know where justice lies, but it doesn't really matter anymore.

00:51:50.710 --> 00:51:51.630
Lord Aoshi...

00:51:51.630 --> 00:51:55.180
Or rather, I want Aoshi Shinomori defeated.

00:51:58.900 --> 00:52:03.780
Aoshi Shinomori, why is it that you have chosen to join us in arms?

00:52:03.990 --> 00:52:05.590
You're mistaken.

00:52:05.770 --> 00:52:13.040
That boy told me that he'd set the stage for me to fight Himura the Battousai without anyone getting in the way.

00:52:13.550 --> 00:52:14.600
That's all.

00:52:14.700 --> 00:52:15.660
Soujiro?

00:52:15.810 --> 00:52:19.320
I did it so we had a stand in for Mr. Chou and Mr. Usui.

00:52:19.870 --> 00:52:21.060
Should I not have done it?

00:52:22.130 --> 00:52:30.000
Probably one who has Shakku's last work will come after us, but I have a different agenda in mind.

00:52:30.660 --> 00:52:32.870
So I'll leave it in your hands to do whatever you'd like to him.

00:52:33.630 --> 00:52:35.920
You're welcome to put some spice into our opening act.

00:52:46.300 --> 00:52:48.520
Guys, listen up!

00:52:48.680 --> 00:52:52.480
From this point on, I'm the Oniwaban group's Commander!

00:52:56.810 --> 00:52:58.030
No way!

00:52:58.180 --> 00:53:03.110
Shishio's group will sail off during the panic of the Great Kyoto Fire.

00:53:03.610 --> 00:53:07.200
So I would ask everyone to prevent any casualties in Kyoto, I do.

00:53:07.630 --> 00:53:10.040
Understood, but-

00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:11.650
What about Shishio's group?

00:53:12.210 --> 00:53:13.080
About that...

00:53:15.390 --> 00:53:17.370
You're doing this on your own again?

00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:18.370
Miss Kaoru.

00:53:18.920 --> 00:53:20.190
I understand.

00:53:20.670 --> 00:53:23.340
I too, along with Miss Misao and with everyone else, will fight here together.

00:53:23.770 --> 00:53:24.610
Therefore...

00:53:25.330 --> 00:53:27.680
Promise that we'll all return to Tokyo together?

00:53:28.110 --> 00:53:29.230
Yes.

00:53:30.340 --> 00:53:31.260
Promise!

00:53:31.910 --> 00:53:37.030
Just remember what will happen if you break your promise.

00:53:39.450 --> 00:53:42.420
Pay no attention to them. They're always like this.

00:53:51.080 --> 00:53:53.160
I fully understand Gramps...

00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:58.880
If Himura was wrong in his actions, he would never be loved by anyone like that.

00:54:00.440 --> 00:54:01.090
If so...

00:54:03.830 --> 00:54:05.070
Lord Aoshi...

00:54:10.790 --> 00:54:12.530
I'm going to change the water.

00:54:16.070 --> 00:54:16.940
It's my turn now.

00:54:18.050 --> 00:54:19.010
But...

00:54:19.410 --> 00:54:23.360
We're going to be protecting Kyoto, which means we're comrades now.

00:54:23.430 --> 00:54:30.240
It's not so easy to become comrades. To trust others is difficult.

00:54:30.560 --> 00:54:32.560
I-I see.

00:54:34.100 --> 00:54:36.740
We'll then how can we earn that trust?

00:54:37.200 --> 00:54:40.620
I know! Why don't we spar against each other.

00:54:41.380 --> 00:54:43.940
You can learn about someone if you spar against them in a sword fight.

00:54:45.050 --> 00:54:48.310
Forgive me. Now really isn't the best time for that.

00:54:50.060 --> 00:54:50.940
You're just like him...

00:54:52.110 --> 00:54:55.910
Himura, I mean...with let's say...

00:54:55.920 --> 00:54:58.720
...your clumsiness and maybe your boldness.

00:54:59.380 --> 00:55:00.520
How do I put it?

00:55:00.810 --> 00:55:04.610
I feel like you've connected with me by speaking straight from your heart.

00:55:05.830 --> 00:55:08.740
Himura trusted and relied on me.

00:55:09.160 --> 00:55:12.030
So I'll put my trust in Himura and you also.

00:55:12.850 --> 00:55:14.610
Let's fight alongside each other.

00:55:14.950 --> 00:55:16.740
Guard duty begins tonight!

00:55:18.560 --> 00:55:21.960
Kuro, Shiro, Masukami, Omine - everyone suit up!

00:55:22.460 --> 00:55:24.340
The Kyoto Oniwaban group is moving out!

00:55:25.810 --> 00:55:30.730
Yahiko, I'm relying on you to protect Miss Misao and Kyoto, I am.

00:55:31.480 --> 00:55:32.170
Yes!

00:55:32.530 --> 00:55:36.310
I'm going to show off the heart of the Kamiya Kasshin style!

00:55:37.010 --> 00:55:39.760
That's right. I have a message for you Kenshin.

00:55:39.980 --> 00:55:41.690
From that old guy, Hiko.

00:55:42.630 --> 00:55:45.080
Seijuro Hiko?

00:55:46.430 --> 00:55:51.110
<i>He has finally obtained what he once lacked in his swordsmanship.</i>

00:55:51.150 --> 00:55:52.270
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:55:52.930 --> 00:55:58.920
<i>Just because you can cut flesh doesn't mean you've truly crossed swords with your opponent.</i>

00:55:59.750 --> 00:56:02.830
<i>Crossing swords allows one to connect with their opponent's heart. </i>

00:56:02.830 --> 00:56:06.460
<i>Otherwise, you cannot truly threaten your foe's life in the true meaning of the word.</i>

00:56:07.360 --> 00:56:08.420
<i>Spirit, skill and discipline.</i>

00:56:08.920 --> 00:56:11.260
<i>These basic concepts are shared in all marital arts.</i>

00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:15.450
<i>With swordsmanship you learn about yourself and the opponent you're facing through your sword.</i>

00:56:15.720 --> 00:56:18.560
<i>Therefore it is essential that one learns from their heart on to control themselves.</i>

00:56:19.930 --> 00:56:23.630
Crossing swords allows one to connect with their opponent's heart...

00:56:24.210 --> 00:56:26.000
That drunk old man...

00:56:26.280 --> 00:56:27.820
Is he really Kenshin's...?

00:56:27.930 --> 00:56:29.290
My Master, that he is.

00:56:29.770 --> 00:56:31.360
Thank you, Yahiko!

00:56:31.650 --> 00:56:33.700
Indeed, that message you delivered was helpful, it was.

00:56:52.550 --> 00:56:55.280
Go, go, go!

00:56:56.960 --> 00:56:59.330
Hey, is Kyoto really going to be okay?

00:56:59.730 --> 00:57:01.030
It's under control.

00:57:02.830 --> 00:57:03.810
What's this?

00:57:04.480 --> 00:57:09.370
Apparently, Fujita, who came from Tokyo, gathered up five hundred police officers.

00:57:10.800 --> 00:57:13.060
Well then, we should be thankful for that then.

00:57:13.780 --> 00:57:18.530
However, it's a spy's job of the Oniwaban group to protect Kyoto, right?

00:57:18.540 --> 00:57:19.540
Yeah!

00:57:28.440 --> 00:57:29.380
Kaoru!

00:57:30.100 --> 00:57:30.960
Yahiko?

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:34.880
<i>Everyone's spirits are on fire!</i>

00:57:42.330 --> 00:57:45.990
Come on Sou, stop looking in awe and lend a hand, will you?

00:57:46.230 --> 00:57:47.100
Yeah, sure.

00:57:54.970 --> 00:57:56.450
So, that's supposed to be me?

00:57:56.850 --> 00:57:59.780
You told me to engrave it with the words <i>Survival of the Fittest.</i>

00:57:59.780 --> 00:58:00.920
That's right.

00:58:01.790 --> 00:58:10.470
If that's so, when you finally die, this Buddhist statue will be a figurehead, which doesn't speak the truth and would reek of lies.

00:58:12.490 --> 00:58:14.650
Was that meant as encouragement?

00:58:15.230 --> 00:58:17.050
No, as a provocation.

00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:21.230
Fallen Monk.

00:58:25.480 --> 00:58:27.250
They're slow, aren't they?

00:58:27.260 --> 00:58:30.490
I thought we could see flames bursting from Kyoto by now.

00:58:31.820 --> 00:58:34.150
They're up against five hundred police officers.

00:58:34.150 --> 00:58:36.320
It's only natural that it's taking longer than expected.

00:58:36.810 --> 00:58:38.910
We don't need to rush.

00:58:39.520 --> 00:58:42.010
The soldiers might be retreating on us too.

00:58:42.670 --> 00:58:45.320
That's unforgivable! They better not betray Lord Shishio!

00:58:45.720 --> 00:58:48.370
If they want to retreat, let them.

00:58:49.280 --> 00:58:52.840
However, I wonder if they would actually do it?

00:58:53.340 --> 00:58:59.660
They know that there's no place in this country that they can run.

00:59:02.060 --> 00:59:05.220
That's why they chose the path to follow me.

00:59:05.640 --> 00:59:06.810
It's that simple.

00:59:07.180 --> 00:59:08.850
I don't care if they betray me.

00:59:09.190 --> 00:59:11.610
They have their own battle.

00:59:11.780 --> 00:59:12.840
Lord Shishio...

00:59:13.570 --> 00:59:14.560
Lord Shishio!

00:59:14.980 --> 00:59:16.500
The blaze has started?

00:59:16.510 --> 00:59:17.370
No, they haven't.

00:59:17.600 --> 00:59:18.990
There's a one horse carriage is approaching!

00:59:19.850 --> 00:59:21.870
Wow I can see something with a cloud of steam.

00:59:21.870 --> 00:59:22.660
You think that's it?

00:59:23.400 --> 00:59:25.260
It doesn't look like a large black ship to me!

00:59:25.590 --> 00:59:26.950
It's as I predicted.

00:59:26.950 --> 00:59:30.580
You couldn't possibly understand the concept of <i>camouflage</i>, rooster head.

00:59:31.330 --> 00:59:32.040
What is that?

00:59:32.440 --> 00:59:35.730
It's an appearance to deceive idiots like yourself.

00:59:35.730 --> 00:59:36.880
I gotcha.

00:59:36.880 --> 00:59:38.630
The Devil found some idle hands to do his dirty work.

00:59:38.860 --> 00:59:42.950
The last of the Shinsengumi has personally come to see us set sail.

00:59:45.110 --> 00:59:49.310
Sorry, but it's not who you're waiting for, Mr. Commander.

00:59:55.070 --> 00:59:58.170
Now then, how are we bombarding this ship?

00:59:58.580 --> 01:00:00.360
We'd never make it swimming there.

01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:01.310
That's for sure.

01:00:01.730 --> 01:00:03.290
I can't let you pass.

01:00:04.200 --> 01:00:07.210
You have to turn around from this point.

01:00:07.670 --> 01:00:11.290
Otherwise, I will have to begin a Buddhist invocation once you are dead.

01:00:12.110 --> 01:00:17.240
Although, I'm not religious, I'm somewhat hesitant about having to kill a monk.

01:00:17.430 --> 01:00:18.930
If that so, then here...

01:00:18.980 --> 01:00:20.140
Leave this to me.

01:00:20.500 --> 01:00:22.770
It seems like there nothing to him at first glance...

01:00:23.290 --> 01:00:25.500
But, this guy should be a good one-on-one match for me.

01:00:26.380 --> 01:00:29.010
Then I'll leave it to you. Don't underestimate him though.

01:00:29.030 --> 01:00:30.000
Right.

01:00:30.360 --> 01:00:33.190
The Devil found some idle hands to do his work, so here comes the flames!

01:00:39.770 --> 01:00:42.520
Damn you! You're a destructive monk!

01:00:46.770 --> 01:00:49.540
It's too early in the season to go swimming in the sea.

01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:51.080
Best of luck to you, Mr. Saito.

01:00:51.300 --> 01:00:52.250
We're going to use <i>it</i> then.

01:00:52.250 --> 01:00:53.370
Sou, come help.

01:00:53.550 --> 01:00:55.060
You mean that thing?

01:00:55.270 --> 01:00:56.270
Move it!

01:00:56.270 --> 01:00:57.100
Yeah, sure!

01:01:01.430 --> 01:01:04.240
Go ahead, turn the handle to fire it.

01:01:05.530 --> 01:01:07.340
Well now, where will you appear?

01:01:09.080 --> 01:01:11.630
Where will you come out from, Hajime Saito?

01:01:24.510 --> 01:01:26.300
Sou, reload the ammo!

01:01:26.450 --> 01:01:27.160
Yeah, sure!

01:01:27.510 --> 01:01:29.380
That's enough for now.

01:01:29.380 --> 01:01:30.380
Lord Shishio?

01:01:30.890 --> 01:01:37.430
If the last of the Shinsengumi got shot and was fed to the fish, it would be embarrassing for him in the heavens.

01:01:37.520 --> 01:01:40.150
The one who'll take care of him, is me.

01:01:40.510 --> 01:01:44.090
Shishio's actions are never contradictory, are they?

01:01:44.090 --> 01:01:46.890
Because of that, we don't need to do anything.

01:01:47.130 --> 01:01:49.280
That makes it easy for us, doesn't it, Miss Yumi?

01:01:56.880 --> 01:01:59.960
Welcome to my ship, Hajime Saito.

01:02:00.900 --> 01:02:04.710
Pleasure to meet you, my name is Makoto Shishio.

01:02:05.340 --> 01:02:10.790
Since my subordinates were so rude to you, allow me to politely show my appreciation for coming to see us off with this sword.

01:02:11.110 --> 01:02:12.310
What do you say?

01:02:13.340 --> 01:02:14.710
I see.

01:02:14.710 --> 01:02:17.710
You have a rank of which solidifies an organization.

01:02:18.470 --> 01:02:21.660
If that's the case, I have to fully accept your offer.

01:02:24.230 --> 01:02:24.960
Come.

01:02:59.090 --> 01:03:01.080
Oh! The two of you took care of things.

01:03:01.460 --> 01:03:03.650
I've summoned the police, so let them take care of the rest.

01:03:03.960 --> 01:03:04.400
Misa-

01:03:04.680 --> 01:03:05.870
Where's the Commander?

01:03:06.320 --> 01:03:06.930
Misa-

01:03:07.550 --> 01:03:09.340
The Commander is doing a good job overseeing us.

01:03:09.800 --> 01:03:11.350
It seems like everything is under control.

01:03:11.330 --> 01:03:13.910
The two of you can probably go back at least once to the Aoiya.

01:03:18.220 --> 01:03:18.940
Misa-

01:03:19.440 --> 01:03:20.060
Commander!

01:03:20.400 --> 01:03:23.770
All flash points have been prevented with the help of the citizens.

01:03:24.650 --> 01:03:26.570
I did well for my first job!

01:03:26.820 --> 01:03:28.610
It's great to think that Kyoto city has been pro-

01:03:29.180 --> 01:03:30.280
Lu No. 1?

01:03:32.230 --> 01:03:34.170
Hang on, what's wrong Lu No. 1?

01:03:34.550 --> 01:03:36.790
You fled? The Aoiya is-?

01:04:01.890 --> 01:04:03.520
That's what I expected from your strength.

01:04:04.020 --> 01:04:05.730
My eyes haven't deceived me at all.

01:04:06.650 --> 01:04:10.890
My greatest obstacle has been you, Hajime Saito!

01:04:11.180 --> 01:04:14.010
However, to be honest, I'm disappointed.

01:04:14.360 --> 01:04:20.710
Even though you have such strength, are called a wolf from Mibu, just why did you become a lapdog of the government?

01:04:21.440 --> 01:04:24.210
Are you satisfied with this era?

01:04:24.650 --> 01:04:30.170
As a wolf without a fangs, what could possibly make you wag your tail in this era?

01:04:31.680 --> 01:04:34.210
Aku Soku Zan!

01:04:34.960 --> 01:04:36.700
Slay Evil Immediately?

01:04:37.270 --> 01:04:38.350
Am I evil?

01:04:38.550 --> 01:04:39.940
What kind of evil then?

01:04:40.170 --> 01:04:42.610
I regard those who are strong as justified.

01:04:42.710 --> 01:04:44.350
The weak are evil.

01:04:44.560 --> 01:04:48.610
Saito your strength is based on your beliefs.

01:04:48.930 --> 01:04:50.660
You and the Battousai is different.

01:04:50.990 --> 01:04:53.260
So which one of your beliefs is right?

01:04:53.260 --> 01:04:55.420
Why don't you bare your fangs and howl!

01:04:57.100 --> 01:04:57.660
Aku...

01:04:58.830 --> 01:04:59.500
...Soku...

01:05:00.220 --> 01:05:00.770
...Zan!

01:05:03.860 --> 01:05:04.580
Gatotsu...

01:05:05.280 --> 01:05:06.200
...Zero Stance!

01:05:12.840 --> 01:05:13.630
Take this!

01:05:16.010 --> 01:05:17.780
It seems we have our answer.

01:05:18.380 --> 01:05:23.050
It was close, but once your fangs are broken,
a wolf and a dog are almost the same.

01:05:23.220 --> 01:05:25.600
My obstacle is now out of my path.

01:05:26.240 --> 01:05:31.170
Yumi, order an increase the steam output in the engine room. We'll depart as soon as Anji boards.

01:05:32.160 --> 01:05:35.570
Saito, I'm bringing you along also.

01:05:35.570 --> 01:05:39.120
I'll show you first hand just how the evil Meiji government will fall.

01:05:39.900 --> 01:05:41.780
Sou, go tend to his wounds.

01:06:14.360 --> 01:06:14.940
Gramps!

01:06:14.940 --> 01:06:15.750
Okina!

01:06:18.390 --> 01:06:19.290
Misao!

01:06:23.530 --> 01:06:24.770
Help us!

01:06:24.770 --> 01:06:25.770
Get out of here!

01:06:27.350 --> 01:06:28.560
It's a monster!

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:31.010
Miss Kaoru?

01:06:41.400 --> 01:06:43.810
Yahiko, we'll take him on simultaneously!

01:06:44.220 --> 01:06:45.850
Don't get distracted with how his sword moves!

01:06:46.110 --> 01:06:46.960
Right!

01:06:47.480 --> 01:06:49.210
Ochika, please take care of Gramps!

01:06:49.580 --> 01:06:49.890
Misa-

01:06:49.890 --> 01:06:50.710
Commander!

01:07:01.110 --> 01:07:04.110
I didn't know that there was such a strong monk around.

01:07:04.720 --> 01:07:09.840
Why are you following Shishio even though you're this strong?

01:07:09.920 --> 01:07:12.740
Even though I am a fallen monk, I am still a monk.

01:07:13.210 --> 01:07:19.730
Though now I've lost faith in God and Buddha, I would lose my role in life if had nothing to pray for.

01:07:19.790 --> 01:07:23.320
I really don't get how much Makoto Shishio is really worth to you?

01:07:23.980 --> 01:07:28.340
I can't allow you to pray for someone who has no understanding to the pain of those who are weak.

01:07:28.890 --> 01:07:29.990
I ain't giving up.

01:07:34.660 --> 01:07:36.960
Lord Shishio, are you okay?

01:07:37.150 --> 01:07:39.580
Yeah, my metal helmet saved me.

01:07:40.240 --> 01:07:41.470
Anji's still not back?

01:07:41.580 --> 01:07:42.040
Yes.

01:07:42.430 --> 01:07:45.040
I wonder if he's still struggling with Saito's comrade?

01:07:45.790 --> 01:07:49.330
Sou is out there, so I think I'll give my body a rest.

01:07:51.880 --> 01:07:53.460
We will wait a while longer.

01:07:54.290 --> 01:07:57.090
It would seem the Commander is still waiting for his man as well.

01:08:01.180 --> 01:08:02.390
Am I not hot?

01:08:03.130 --> 01:08:04.590
I don't mind it.

01:08:05.310 --> 01:08:10.990
The illusion and desire for peace seems to be a dream that cannot be met in this era.

01:08:11.590 --> 01:08:16.970
Yet you are a man who showed me a dream from which I shall never awaken.

01:08:33.680 --> 01:08:35.150
Yahiko, get down!

01:08:41.070 --> 01:08:43.310
Mr. Saito you're pretty strong aren't you?

01:08:43.390 --> 01:08:45.350
That technique was the Gatotsu.

01:08:45.550 --> 01:08:47.760
For a second there I thought it was all over.

01:08:48.760 --> 01:08:51.740
When those injuries heal, I would like to fight you.

01:08:52.230 --> 01:08:56.350
We'll have to do it later though as I promised the same thing to Mr. Himura.

01:08:56.440 --> 01:08:58.260
<i>If </i>you defeat him, that is.

01:08:59.070 --> 01:09:01.450
You hold Mr. Himura in high regard, don't you?

01:09:01.840 --> 01:09:05.690
After all, it's probably natural since he was a worthy opponent during revolution.

01:09:05.790 --> 01:09:09.320
Since you've crossed blades with him, you should already be aware of that.

01:09:09.660 --> 01:09:12.010
Yet you still remain clueless.

01:09:14.050 --> 01:09:16.150
You intend to fight him again, right?

01:09:17.170 --> 01:09:19.720
Well, the wait is finally over.

01:09:31.830 --> 01:09:33.060
Gramps, get out of here!

01:09:44.730 --> 01:09:46.540
Yahiko, get out of there!

01:09:46.760 --> 01:09:47.840
Yahiko!

01:09:48.120 --> 01:09:51.500
Kenshin asked us to take care of things here for him.

01:09:51.770 --> 01:09:54.010
That's why I'm not moving a single step!

01:09:54.570 --> 01:09:55.470
I ain't moving!

01:09:56.100 --> 01:09:58.030
Y-Yahiko run for it!

01:10:00.180 --> 01:10:02.160
This is it.

01:10:10.660 --> 01:10:12.650
I found you, boy.

01:10:12.930 --> 01:10:13.600
Old man!

01:10:14.880 --> 01:10:16.710
It's a reverse-blade sword!

01:10:19.670 --> 01:10:24.680
Mr. Shakku must have been out of his mind in his final days to forge a reverse-blade sword that cannot kill.

01:10:25.450 --> 01:10:27.610
If you are strong you live, if you are weak you die.

01:10:27.610 --> 01:10:30.080
Even I can't overlook something as simple as that.

01:10:30.080 --> 01:10:31.410
That blade is a mistake.

01:10:32.400 --> 01:10:36.270
I'm always thinking about how well matched you are with that sword, since you always hesitate.

01:10:36.420 --> 01:10:37.710
I will not let go of my hesitation.

01:10:38.130 --> 01:10:41.710
It was because of my hesitation that I have met these people.

01:10:44.720 --> 01:10:46.430
Seijuro Hiko...

01:10:47.460 --> 01:10:49.730
You took off too soon!

01:10:51.940 --> 01:10:53.940
I expected you to repay your debt!

01:10:54.140 --> 01:10:58.340
You'll have to work hard to cover the cost of the pot you broke!

01:11:00.360 --> 01:11:03.040
What the heck are you talking about, old man, especially during a time like this?

01:11:03.650 --> 01:11:06.480
It would seem your debt is about to grow again.

01:11:07.570 --> 01:11:10.300
A body like that has quite a bit of excessive force.

01:11:10.530 --> 01:11:15.870
There will be a lot of tension under the armor if you can not master wearing it.

01:11:16.280 --> 01:11:21.950
Even if you do not have the will to fight, you take any instinct you have with you into battle.

01:11:21.960 --> 01:11:24.960
He came to Shishio, who had accepted that about him.

01:11:25.340 --> 01:11:27.300
I shall put your suffering to an end.

01:11:27.680 --> 01:11:31.790
Even with all your strength, you can not defeat
this man standing in front of you.

01:11:32.600 --> 01:11:33.640
It's all right.

01:11:34.140 --> 01:11:37.060
Go ahead. Show us your true self.

01:12:02.190 --> 01:12:03.530
Let's begin then.

01:12:27.190 --> 01:12:29.690
Your new sword is impressive.

01:12:30.320 --> 01:12:32.950
You've even improved on your agility to keep up with me.

01:12:33.470 --> 01:12:37.250
It's strange that even though you, Mr. Himura, are now no longer the Battousai...

01:12:37.280 --> 01:12:40.960
...that you could be so strong and still use a sword that doesn't kill?

01:12:43.830 --> 01:12:46.100
What Mr. Saito said, irritates me also.

01:12:46.410 --> 01:12:47.770
It irritates me a lot.

01:12:48.800 --> 01:12:50.590
I don't want to you acknowledge you.

01:12:51.130 --> 01:12:53.470
Hesitation must never defeat conviction!

01:12:53.720 --> 01:12:54.800
It must not!

01:13:06.520 --> 01:13:07.880
I'm coming for real this time.

01:13:34.130 --> 01:13:34.800
I can win!

01:13:35.500 --> 01:13:36.090
I will defeat you!

01:13:43.830 --> 01:13:45.320
But why...?

01:13:46.030 --> 01:13:49.990
<i>This one</i> couldn't read your movements before because you have no emotions.

01:13:50.340 --> 01:13:52.720
However, as your emotions are now...

01:13:53.450 --> 01:13:54.760
I see.

01:13:55.780 --> 01:14:00.920
Mr. Himura, you used your sword to read my emotions, which have awoken, and thus led me to my defeat.

01:14:01.590 --> 01:14:05.850
You've obtained a different kind of strength than the one you possessed when you were Battousai.

01:14:06.250 --> 01:14:08.400
Even though I was clueless, I can finally understand.

01:14:09.230 --> 01:14:12.440
However, that will not work on Mr. Shishio.

01:14:13.110 --> 01:14:17.380
Mr. Shishio incinerates all life without hesitation.

01:14:17.740 --> 01:14:21.380
The color of his heart is like a black flame.

01:14:21.700 --> 01:14:22.850
He's crying.

01:14:23.110 --> 01:14:24.770
Seijuro Hiko...

01:14:32.860 --> 01:14:39.780
He could see his sadness as an unfulfilled warrior through that monstrous appearance.

01:14:40.740 --> 01:14:42.620
What an incredible man.

01:14:43.290 --> 01:14:44.660
A warriors sadness.

01:14:44.960 --> 01:14:47.500
The same is also true of Shishio.

01:14:49.060 --> 01:14:54.300
Everyone who has gathered under Shishio has been left at the mercy of the imperial extremists.

01:14:54.300 --> 01:14:57.380
They have been hurt in both body and mind.

01:14:58.010 --> 01:15:00.430
That is precisely why they depend on his strength.

01:15:00.720 --> 01:15:02.060
They depend on his power.

01:15:02.560 --> 01:15:03.430
And thus...

01:15:04.670 --> 01:15:06.140
We seek the light that is no longer there.

01:15:11.810 --> 01:15:13.000
The light?

01:15:13.300 --> 01:15:16.330
You really think that Shishio is that?

01:15:16.960 --> 01:15:22.590
As a monk who is forever seeking salvation, to suffer does not mean there will be an end to it.

01:15:22.900 --> 01:15:25.590
You think you'll find salvation through destruction?

01:15:26.180 --> 01:15:28.870
If it is the will of the Shinto and Buddhist gods, then we have to accept it.

01:15:29.250 --> 01:15:31.130
But this is not something that people can decide!

01:15:32.110 --> 01:15:34.220
This kind of salvation is unacceptable!

01:15:50.850 --> 01:15:52.730
I... understand now.

01:15:54.610 --> 01:15:56.230
I can tell, when we throw our punches.

01:15:56.780 --> 01:15:57.650
Tell what?

01:15:58.240 --> 01:15:59.110
I got it...

01:15:59.820 --> 01:16:00.740
You...

01:16:01.160 --> 01:16:03.740
I believe <i>you</i> are the light for Shishio.

01:16:04.370 --> 01:16:06.790
Shishio is searching for salvation.

01:16:08.050 --> 01:16:14.700
Makoto Shishio... isn't seeking his own salvation.

01:16:14.920 --> 01:16:18.090
He's attempting to burn like a flame that will allow him to rebuild this era.

01:16:18.970 --> 01:16:21.340
He would use himself as the tinder...

01:16:21.930 --> 01:16:24.180
At this rate, Makoto Shishio will...

01:16:26.600 --> 01:16:28.270
What about your light?

01:16:29.570 --> 01:16:30.730
My light...

01:16:31.440 --> 01:16:37.110
For a guy like me, who lost all faith in everything...

01:16:37.900 --> 01:16:40.900
...there was someone there with the desire to pull me back to believe again.

01:16:50.830 --> 01:16:53.210
This is the signal that indicates that Lord Shishio is setting sail to victory.

01:16:54.080 --> 01:16:54.960
Make it impressive!

01:17:02.130 --> 01:17:06.180
Makoto Shishio once said, <i>Our world is a living Hell.</i>

01:17:07.760 --> 01:17:12.310
While in Hell, he would don the flames of truth...

01:17:12.390 --> 01:17:14.770
...and thrust forward with a large ironclad warship.

01:17:15.360 --> 01:17:16.650
A-A black ship?

01:17:17.230 --> 01:17:17.860
That is...

01:17:25.740 --> 01:17:26.830
...The Purgatory.

01:17:33.540 --> 01:17:34.410
The Purgatory.

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:37.010
Welcome to the Purgatory.

01:17:37.890 --> 01:17:41.260
You beat Soujiro with Shakku's last work.

01:17:41.260 --> 01:17:42.260
How interesting!

01:17:42.810 --> 01:17:47.320
I had prepared an opening act for you, but it seems that you have some injuries.

01:17:47.320 --> 01:17:51.500
Why don't we skip to the main show: a battle between brother swords, my predecessor?

01:17:51.670 --> 01:17:55.940
That is the reason why <i>this one</i> has come with this sword too.

01:17:55.950 --> 01:17:59.350
The ship has set sail. We will all go to Tokyo together.

01:17:59.690 --> 01:18:06.140
By the time we reach Tokyo, I wonder which of our corpses will have taken the helm?

01:18:10.970 --> 01:18:13.020
Now that looks like a true warrior!

01:18:13.260 --> 01:18:16.870
Somehow, he managed to connect with that man's heart.

01:18:17.230 --> 01:18:18.400
His heart?

01:18:18.680 --> 01:18:20.680
The Mugenjin, Homura.

01:18:20.680 --> 01:18:23.940
This is the name of my sword that Shakku forged.

01:18:24.830 --> 01:18:25.780
Mugen...

01:18:25.790 --> 01:18:30.050
Infinite: a promise of continuing and an unending path to victory.

01:18:30.360 --> 01:18:31.970
The reverse-blade sword, Keishin...

01:18:32.230 --> 01:18:36.170
This sword was forged with the ideals that Sir Shakku held dear to him.

01:18:36.450 --> 01:18:41.570
If that's so, then his desires were nothing more than a hell on earth of which he rolled in bloody mud!

01:18:52.160 --> 01:18:57.710
<i>Kenshin, will you be able to connect with Shishio's heart?</i>

01:19:24.730 --> 01:19:28.500
You can't defeat me with a reverse-blade sword, my predecessor.

01:19:29.260 --> 01:19:31.140
A sword is meant to kill people!

01:19:31.910 --> 01:19:36.210
If you hope to defeat me, turn the blade on your sword and become the Battousai once again!

01:19:39.330 --> 01:19:40.710
I will not turn my blade.

01:19:41.330 --> 01:19:45.420
This sword embodies the deepest hopes for peace in this era.

01:19:46.280 --> 01:19:48.550
This world cannot change through your ideals.

01:19:48.550 --> 01:19:51.760
You will only be devoured by the law of <i>Survival of the Fittest.</i>

01:19:56.850 --> 01:19:58.220
So they made it just in time.

01:20:01.170 --> 01:20:03.920
Adjust the angle to compensate! Reload again!

01:20:04.530 --> 01:20:06.660
<i>Saito, don't die.</i>

01:20:06.820 --> 01:20:09.790
Do not let that ship leave the bay! Fire!

01:20:15.650 --> 01:20:18.750
It seems the government dogs are doing a good job.

01:20:19.400 --> 01:20:21.900
Yumi, get the ship turned, and respond accordingly.

01:20:22.090 --> 01:20:25.380
Sou, likely the army's attack is coming from a summit on Mount Tenpo.

01:20:25.700 --> 01:20:27.500
Counterattack with everything!

01:20:27.740 --> 01:20:29.140
Turn-a-port.

01:20:34.360 --> 01:20:37.430
Elevate the angle! That should do it!

01:20:37.660 --> 01:20:40.380
Four! Three! Two! Commence fire!

01:20:40.380 --> 01:20:41.370
Begin!

01:20:46.960 --> 01:20:49.520
Don't stop! Continue attacking!

01:21:02.970 --> 01:21:04.680
Tokyo will suffer the same results.

01:21:05.020 --> 01:21:06.770
That is the power of the Purgatory.

01:21:18.600 --> 01:21:19.430
<i>This is the Engine Room. </i>

01:21:19.720 --> 01:21:21.310
<i>The cannons are making the engine gush steam.</i>

01:21:21.680 --> 01:21:23.310
<i>We can't get to it with the high temperatures!</i>

01:21:23.750 --> 01:21:25.240
<i>Hurry and shut it down!</i>

01:21:26.810 --> 01:21:31.380
My predecessor, it must be karma for the terrible things we have done...

01:21:31.680 --> 01:21:34.280
...because we never seem to have much luck when we need it the most.

01:21:36.220 --> 01:21:39.300
Can you feel how I boil, my predecessor?

01:21:49.530 --> 01:21:50.960
I will not die!

01:21:51.770 --> 01:21:53.240
I am strong!

01:21:54.340 --> 01:21:58.530
<i>Even if you manage to connect with someone's heart, you cannot win if your opponent devours your heart.</i>

01:21:59.020 --> 01:22:01.030
<i>Can you win, Kenshin?</i>

01:22:30.040 --> 01:22:31.860
Lord Shishio!!!

01:22:50.650 --> 01:22:51.670
The light...

01:22:52.420 --> 01:22:53.740
The light connected with him...?

01:22:54.280 --> 01:22:57.050
Crossing swords allows one to connect with their opponent's heart.

01:23:18.890 --> 01:23:24.970
<i>It was this one's job to fight, but somewhere along the line, I forced the tainted name of a manslayer on Shishio.</i>

01:23:25.680 --> 01:23:29.850
<i>But now... this one shall accept the taint unto this one's self...</i>

01:23:30.440 --> 01:23:33.020
<i>A taint needed to protect a world of peace.</i>

01:23:33.820 --> 01:23:35.360
Hurry, let's get out of here! Abandon ship!

01:23:43.370 --> 01:23:44.590
I've been waiting...

01:23:48.260 --> 01:23:53.910
On a sinking ship where everyone is about to die, no one shall interfere.

01:23:54.380 --> 01:23:56.670
We will settle things here.

01:23:57.290 --> 01:24:01.710
Because of you I lost my comrades... I have lost <i>everything.</i>

01:24:02.720 --> 01:24:03.890
I will defeat you.

01:24:04.260 --> 01:24:08.140
And the title of the strongest will be the flower that I take to their graves.

01:24:08.810 --> 01:24:10.020
You have not lost everything.

01:24:10.230 --> 01:24:14.360
There are still a young woman who is praying and hoping for your safe return.

01:24:14.780 --> 01:24:18.650
I was asked by that young woman... to defeat you.

01:24:20.200 --> 01:24:23.620
If we could have connected with his heart...

01:24:24.490 --> 01:24:26.790
Could this have turned out differently, Gramps?

01:24:27.660 --> 01:24:30.080
Connected with Lord Aoshi's heart...

01:24:31.080 --> 01:24:34.710
<i>This one</i> cannot grant Miss Misao's wish.

01:24:35.090 --> 01:24:38.630
So I will return the old Aoshi Shinomori back to her side.

01:24:39.670 --> 01:24:43.010
But first, there is the Aoshi Shinomori before me who is struggling in darkness.

01:24:43.090 --> 01:24:49.640
I must cut away the these delusions that 
Miss Misao hates with my reverse-blade sword, Keishin!

01:24:51.620 --> 01:24:52.020
Hey.

01:24:52.310 --> 01:24:53.220
Mr. Saito.

01:24:53.770 --> 01:24:57.150
If the fire gets to the ammunition lying around here, this ship is going to explode into pieces.

01:24:57.440 --> 01:25:00.950
I would rather be gone before that happens, but I can't row the boat with my legs in this condition.

01:25:01.490 --> 01:25:03.070
That's why, I want you to take me to the shore.

01:25:04.910 --> 01:25:05.770
Yeah, sure.

01:25:49.200 --> 01:25:51.730
Mi...sao...

01:26:07.420 --> 01:26:08.280
Kenshin!

01:26:17.490 --> 01:26:19.510
Lord Shishio, look...

01:26:20.380 --> 01:26:21.770
It's burning...

01:26:22.310 --> 01:26:25.700
Our world is burning so brilliantly.

01:26:28.920 --> 01:26:32.440
Everything turned out as you had hoped.

01:26:44.170 --> 01:26:46.290
I really envy Miss Yumi...

01:26:46.690 --> 01:26:48.810
I'm the only one who got left behind.

01:26:50.000 --> 01:26:52.590
It's all because of you Mr. Saito... geez.

01:26:53.890 --> 01:26:56.180
The black ship... The Purgatory is sinking.

01:26:56.910 --> 01:26:57.480
Yeah.

01:26:58.150 --> 01:26:59.650
Tokyo has been protected.

01:27:00.480 --> 01:27:01.520
As for what's next...

01:27:26.760 --> 01:27:30.300
In the end, the only thing that burned in the so called Great Kyoto Fire was this place.

01:27:30.700 --> 01:27:32.610
Good thing there wasn't much damage.

01:27:32.840 --> 01:27:34.040
It's not good at all!

01:27:34.040 --> 01:27:34.930
Now, now...

01:27:35.200 --> 01:27:36.120
Oh? Kenshin!

01:27:36.510 --> 01:27:37.860
Aoshi?

01:27:43.270 --> 01:27:44.720
Aoshi.

01:27:50.030 --> 01:27:50.910
Ao...

01:27:57.330 --> 01:27:59.580
Lord Aoshi!!!

01:28:01.650 --> 01:28:02.450
Kenshin.

01:28:07.490 --> 01:28:08.720
Welcome home!

01:28:10.600 --> 01:28:11.580
I'm back.

01:28:12.800 --> 01:28:14.080
Now that I think about it...

01:28:14.090 --> 01:28:15.780
Where did Mr. Hiko go?

01:28:19.020 --> 01:28:20.850
<i>I guess I'll be celebrating tonight.</i>

01:28:41.490 --> 01:28:44.180
The Mugenjin Homura...

01:28:44.430 --> 01:28:49.510
While my father wanted peaceful times he
continued to forge killing swords.

01:28:50.570 --> 01:28:55.790
This sword and that contradiction to his belief will remain here as an offering.

01:29:00.720 --> 01:29:01.760
Here.

01:29:02.800 --> 01:29:05.880
That, please keep it if you would.

01:29:06.240 --> 01:29:07.600
Sir Seiku.

01:29:07.930 --> 01:29:10.950
So long as you have that reverse-blade sword, my father's ideals live on.

01:29:11.700 --> 01:29:13.320
I know that you understand that!

01:29:16.700 --> 01:29:18.780
I gratefully accept you lending it to me, I do.

01:29:18.920 --> 01:29:20.220
Himura!

01:29:20.760 --> 01:29:24.060
When the times of peace have come, and the reverse-blade sword is not needed...

01:29:24.060 --> 01:29:26.540
And my oath never to kill again isn't necessary.

01:29:26.540 --> 01:29:31.360
When that time comes, someday alongside the Homura...

01:29:31.360 --> 01:29:35.970
...I'll have the reverse-blade sword to rest forever with it, I shall.

01:29:36.550 --> 01:29:38.020
Shell!

01:29:39.830 --> 01:29:40.810
Shell?

01:29:41.560 --> 01:29:42.780
Those are Himura's words.

01:29:43.020 --> 01:29:47.180
Shell! Shell! Himura shell!

01:30:25.280 --> 01:30:33.610
There are answers that are missing some pieces

01:30:34.010 --> 01:30:40.410
It's not enough just to know the correct answers

01:30:41.830 --> 01:30:49.790
I tried to match the pieces but they didn't pair up

01:30:50.390 --> 01:30:51.700
I feel so!

01:30:51.710 --> 01:30:59.710
The scenery looks kind when I'm fulfilled

01:30:59.710 --> 01:31:07.410
Just like the same things you see in your eyes

01:31:07.640 --> 01:31:09.300
Forever, right?

01:31:09.360 --> 01:31:16.930
Don't go away, begin a new life

01:31:17.280 --> 01:31:26.430
Put it in words and then sing it out loud

01:31:26.930 --> 01:31:29.630
Let me stay close to you

01:31:29.830 --> 01:31:36.140
My heart has been taken

01:31:36.380 --> 01:31:46.880
This desperation has been caused by the colorful winds

01:31:46.880 --> 01:31:48.540
I feel you!

01:31:48.540 --> 01:31:56.430
The scenery looks kind when I'm fulfilled

01:31:56.430 --> 01:32:04.270
Just like the kind of things you reflect in your back

01:32:04.670 --> 01:32:06.080
Ain't there more?

01:32:06.080 --> 01:32:13.880
Give me more bright feelings when I wake up

01:32:14.170 --> 01:32:23.430
Put it in words and then sing it out loud
